# .secretscanignore
#
# Tells the scanner what to skip. Two rule types:
#
#   file:<pattern>    -> skip an entire file (supports * wildcards)
#   string:<exact>     -> skip one exact matched string, wherever it appears
#
# Use file: for things that are never going to contain real secrets
# (docs, test fixtures). Use string: when you've manually reviewed a
# specific flagged value and confirmed it's safe.

# README contains a long image-banner URL and an example output
# section, both of which produce high-entropy false positives.
file:README.md

# test_samples/ holds intentionally fake secrets used to test the
# scanner itself -- these are supposed to look like real secrets, so
# they'll always be "found", which is correct, not a false positive.
# Uncomment if you'd rather the scanner not report on its own fixtures:
# file:test_samples/*
